sentences.t:
[unde locum Grai dixerunt nomine Aornon.]
quattuor hic primum nigrantis terga iuvencos
constituit, frontique invergit vina sacerdos;

sentences.l:
[whence the place the Greeks called by the name Aornos.]
four here first, black-backed, bullocks
she sets in place, and on the brow tips wine, the priestess;

sentences.t:
Di, quibus imperium est animarum, umbraeque silentes,
et Chaos, et Phlegethon, loca nocte tacentia late,
sit mihi fas audita loqui;

sentences.l:
Gods, to whom the rule is of souls, and shades silent,
and Chaos, and Phlegethon, places in night silent far and wide,
may it be right for me things heard to tell;
